<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Example cases in spatial analysis. The interpretation with less concept-relevance is in <span id="S5.T3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">italic</span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The complete experimental and analytical results of each model can be found in the Appendix <a href="#S7" title="7 Appendix ‣ Unveiling LLMs’ Metaphorical Understanding: Exploring Conceptual Irrelevance, Context Leveraging and Syntactic Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Conceptual Irrelevance</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Spatial analysis aims to avoid the potential uncertainty of multiple-choice experiment in LLMs’ metaphor interpretation. To validate this problem, we conducted a multiple-choice task: LLMs were tasked with generating two sentences {<math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{21}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{22}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>22</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{22}</annotation></semantics></math>} that matched the meanings of references <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and metaphor <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. {<math id="S5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{21}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{22}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>22</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{22}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>}, were grouped in random order as possible answers for interpretation of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. LLMs were required to select the correct answer. As shown in Appendix <a href="#S7.SS2" title="7.2 Multi-choice Validation Experiment ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Unveiling LLMs’ Metaphorical Understanding: Exploring Conceptual Irrelevance, Context Leveraging and Syntactic Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>, all seven models yielded an accuracy of approximately 50%, indicating multiple-choice tasks can be unreliable in evaluating LLMs in metaphor interpretation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To validate the effectiveness of <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, we introduce an additional measure <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Ad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Ad</annotation></semantics></math>, the sum of cosine similarities between the metaphor interpretation <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and references {<math id="S5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>}. Intuitively, interpretations exhibiting high semantic congruence with both references are expected to have higher respective similarities, <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Ad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Ad</annotation></semantics></math>, with greater probability to be closer to the concept mapping (lower <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>). For V3-671B and Qwen-T, Figure <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 5 Results &amp; Analysis ‣ Unveiling LLMs’ Metaphorical Understanding: Exploring Conceptual Irrelevance, Context Leveraging and Syntactic Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> demonstrated that the <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> to conceptual plane, along with <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Ad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Ad</annotation></semantics></math>, exhibited a mean Spearman’s correlation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Spearman (1961)</a></cite> of <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>= -0.62. The <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\theta</annotation></semantics></math> metric, computing the angle between interpretation plane and the conceptual plane, exhibited a correlation of <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>= -0.64 with <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, collectively validate <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\theta</annotation></semantics></math> as effective quantifiers of conceptual irrelevance.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As summarized in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2 Models ‣ 4 Experiment ‣ Unveiling LLMs’ Metaphorical Understanding: Exploring Conceptual Irrelevance, Context Leveraging and Syntactic Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, GPT-4o achieved the lowest <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> value, indicating its superior ability to suppress irrelevant errors in interpretation at the single-utterance level. Meanwhile, <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\theta</annotation></semantics></math> highlighted holistic discrepancies between interpretation plane and conceptual plane, with V3-671B achieving the best performance. However, it revealed that concept-irrelevant information persists in 15%–25% of the output across all tested LLMs. While LLMs can generate interpretations of metaphors, there are still significant challenges in achieving deeper conceptual domain understanding. This further underscores the need for advancements in metaphor processing, particularly in aligning outputs at concept-level rather than superficial lexical mappings. In Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5 Results &amp; Analysis ‣ Unveiling LLMs’ Metaphorical Understanding: Exploring Conceptual Irrelevance, Context Leveraging and Syntactic Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we present several metaphor interpretations generated by LLMs, including those that accurately capture the concept mapping as well as those exhibiting noticeable deviations with references. Notably, this analysis explicitly excluded preset or fine-tuned models, focusing on the native cognitive capacities of LLMs. A consistent embedding model encoding outputs of all LLMs ensures the variance can only attributed to interpretations.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T4" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S5.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T4.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;"></td>
<th id="S5.T4.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">V3-671B</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen-T</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPT-4</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPT-4o</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.2.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">o3-mini</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.2.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">R1-671B</span></th>
