<span class="ltx_bibblock"><a href="https://proceedings.mlr.press/v139/zhao21c.html" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">Calibrate before use: Improving few-shot performance of language models</a>.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">In <em id="bib.bib46.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proceedings of the 38th International Conference on Machine Learning</em>, volume 139 of <em id="bib.bib46.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proceedings of Machine Learning Research</em>, pages 12697–12706. PMLR.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Appendix</h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the terminologies and definitions included in this paper, the specific prompt settings, as well as the visualization results for each model and experiment.</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.1 </span>Definition and Terminology</h3>

<div id="S7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This paper requires multiple definitions and terminologies to explain the motivation and support our experimental design. Thus, in Table <a href="#S7.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ 7.7 Overlap Ratio of Imagination Word Sets ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Unveiling LLMs’ Metaphorical Understanding: Exploring Conceptual Irrelevance, Context Leveraging and Syntactic Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and Table <a href="#S7.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ 7.7 Overlap Ratio of Imagination Word Sets ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Unveiling LLMs’ Metaphorical Understanding: Exploring Conceptual Irrelevance, Context Leveraging and Syntactic Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we present a detailed compilation of terminologies and definitions mentioned in the paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.2 </span>Multi-choice Validation Experiment</h3>

<div id="S7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to explore the effectiveness of multi-choice experimental settings in metaphor understanding, we conduct the validation experiment. In Fig-QA dataset, the two metaphors {<math id="S7.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>} in one group describe the identical concept with different meanings. Therefore, from {<math id="S7.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{21}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{22}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>22</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{22}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>} (<math id="S7.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{22}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>22</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{22}</annotation></semantics></math> are two sentences generated by LLMs with the identical meaning of <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>), we deploy LLMs to choose the most appropriate interpretation for <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The example of experiment and the accuracy of multi-choice validation are shown in Table <a href="#S7.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ 7.7 Overlap Ratio of Imagination Word Sets ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Unveiling LLMs’ Metaphorical Understanding: Exploring Conceptual Irrelevance, Context Leveraging and Syntactic Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.3 </span>Prompts of Spatial Analysis</h3>

<div id="S7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Two prompts in Figure <a href="#S7.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 7.7 Overlap Ratio of Imagination Word Sets ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Unveiling LLMs’ Metaphorical Understanding: Exploring Conceptual Irrelevance, Context Leveraging and Syntactic Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> are designed for the spatial analysis experiment. Prompt 1 is intended to generate a synonymous sentence <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> aligning with predefined standard literal sentences; prompt 2 instructs models to generate the literal interpretation <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of given metaphor <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, by substituting metaphorical component with literal expression.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.4 </span>Prompts of Metaphorical Imagination</h3>

<div id="S7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Prompts in Figure <a href="#S7.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 7.7 Overlap Ratio of Imagination Word Sets ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Unveiling LLMs’ Metaphorical Understanding: Exploring Conceptual Irrelevance, Context Leveraging and Syntactic Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> are designed for metaphorical imagination. LLMs are required to perform based on the given prompts, to imagine both with and without context: 1) the literal words corresponding to given metaphorical words, and 2) the metaphorical words corresponding to given literal words. Prompts are subdivided into two types, depending on whether contexts are provided in the experiment.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.5 </span>The Prompt of Syntactic Shuffle</h3>

<div id="S7.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">LLMs detect metaphors through the prompt in Figure <a href="#S7.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ 7.7 Overlap Ratio of Imagination Word Sets ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Unveiling LLMs’ Metaphorical Understanding: Exploring Conceptual Irrelevance, Context Leveraging and Syntactic Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> in syntactic shuffle experiment.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.6 </span>Distribution of (<math id="S7.SS6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.SS6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\theta</annotation></semantics></math>) and (<math id="S7.SS6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.SS6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Ad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Ad</annotation></semantics></math>)</h3>

<div id="S7.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present the distance <math id="S7.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> between generated interpretation <math id="S7.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and conceptual plane <math id="S7.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of each metaphor, respectively correlated with <math id="S7.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\theta</annotation></semantics></math> of interpretation and conceptual plane {<math id="S7.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>}, and the sum <math id="S7.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Ad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Ad</annotation></semantics></math> of similarity between interpretation and standard references in Figure <a href="#S7.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ 7.7 Overlap Ratio of Imagination Word Sets ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Unveiling LLMs’ Metaphorical Understanding: Exploring Conceptual Irrelevance, Context Leveraging and Syntactic Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>–<a href="#S7.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ 7.7 Overlap Ratio of Imagination Word Sets ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Unveiling LLMs’ Metaphorical Understanding: Exploring Conceptual Irrelevance, Context Leveraging and Syntactic Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.7 </span>Overlap Ratio of Imagination Word Sets</h3>

<div id="S7.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the metaphorical imagination experiment, we analyze the overlap ratio distribution within imagination word sets, the distribution of overlap ratio under each task and each genre is shown in Figure <a href="#S7.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ 7.7 Overlap Ratio of Imagination Word Sets ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Unveiling LLMs’ Metaphorical Understanding: Exploring Conceptual Irrelevance, Context Leveraging and Syntactic Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>–<a href="#S7.F20" title="Figure 20 ‣ 7.7 Overlap Ratio of Imagination Word Sets ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Unveiling LLMs’ Metaphorical Understanding: Exploring Conceptual Irrelevance, Context Leveraging and Syntactic Influence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>. The portion of different overlap ratios reveals the metaphorical imagination results of LLMs, where a higher overlap ratio (especially 1) suggests that the LLM’s metaphor analysis is detached from the context.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S7.T6" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S7.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S7.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S7.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S7.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Terminology</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S7.T6.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.T6.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S7.T6.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.T6.2.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Notes/Examples</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S7.T6.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T6.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Selection Preference Violation (SPV) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wilks (1975)</a></cite></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T6.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">The disparity between the context of a word within a sentence and its frequently used contexts is an indicator of this word’s metaphorical usage <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tian et al. (2024)</a></cite>.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T6.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">I <span id="S7.T6.2.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">drank</span> a bottle of water.</span>
<span id="S7.T6.2.2.3.1.2" class="ltx_p">Cars <span id="S7.T6.2.2.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">drink</span> gasoline.</span>
<span id="S7.T6.2.2.3.1.3" class="ltx_p">(Drinking usually connected with human, not car.)</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T6.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T6.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Metaphor Identification Procedure (MIP) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Group (2007)</a></cite></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T6.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">A metaphor is identified if the contextual meaning of the word differs from its basic meaning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tian et al. (2024)</a></cite>.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T6.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">They <span id="S7.T6.2.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">fall</span> in love.</span>
<span id="S7.T6.2.3.3.1.2" class="ltx_p">Metaphorical: obsessed in feelings</span>
<span id="S7.T6.2.3.3.1.3" class="ltx_p">Literal: dropping down</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T6.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T6.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Conceptual Metaphor Theory (CMT) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lakoff and Johnson (1980)</a></cite></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T6.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Metaphors are mappings between source domain (describes tangible objects or concepts) and target domain (represents abstract ideas).</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T6.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Metaphor: The arm race.</span>
<span id="S7.T6.2.4.3.1.2" class="ltx_p">Source domain: COMPETITION</span>
<span id="S7.T6.2.4.3.1.3" class="ltx_p">Target domain:
ARMS BUILDUP</span>
<span id="S7.T6.2.4.3.1.4" class="ltx_p">Conceptual mapping: COMPETITION IS ARMS BUILDUP</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T6.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T6.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Multiple Metaphor-Literal Mappings across Domains</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T6.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">A pair of source
and target domains can encompass multiple metaphorical mappings. The same meaning in metaphor can be expressed through multiple comparison of metaphorical and literal indication.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T6.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">The mapping “thinking is linguistic activity”
can be the generic concept of “memorization is writing” or
“ideas are word”.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T6.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T6.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Trigger Word Error <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wachowiak and Gromann (2023)</a></cite></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T6.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">The model predict wrong source domains that were not metaphorically related, because models only infer from the words that are commonly co-occurred instead of considering context.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T6.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">The conceptual mapping
of “The arms race.” is falsely identified as COMPETITION
IS WAR, due to the commonly co-occurrence of “arm” and
“war” in daily discourse.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T6.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T6.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Concept-irrelevant Error/Conceptual Irrelevance</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T6.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">The interpretation generated by LLMs failed to clarify the actual target domain that
source domain intended to map.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T6.2.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.7.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.7.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Interpreting falling in
love as physically falling rather than entering an emotional
state.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T6.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T6.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Context Leveraging</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T6.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.8.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Leveraging holistic context when analyzing metaphor rather than focusing on specific words.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T6.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.8.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T6.2.8.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Metaphor: The arm race.</span>
<span id="S7.T6.2.8.3.1.2" class="ltx_p">Conceptual mapping: COMPETITION IS ARMS BUILDUP</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Terminology and definitions related to metaphor identification and context analysis in this study (Part 1).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<figure id="S7.T7" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S7.T7.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S7.T7.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S7.T7.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S7.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Terminology</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S7.T7.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.T7.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S7.T7.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.T7.2.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Notes/Examples</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S7.T7.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T7.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Conceptual Plane <math id="S7.T7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T7.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Constructed by the embeddings of three
sentences <math id="S7.T7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.T7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.T7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, implying correct concept mapping. Representing the ideal concept the metaphor intended to convey.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T7.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S7.T7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>: The computer runs fast.</span>
<span id="S7.T7.2.2.3.1.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="S7.T7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>: The computer runs slow.</span>
<span id="S7.T7.2.2.3.1.3" class="ltx_p"><math id="S7.T7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>: The computer processes fast.</span>
<span id="S7.T7.2.2.3.1.4" class="ltx_p">The conceptual plane include the concept of the speed of computers.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T7.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T7.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Interpretation Plane <math id="S7.T7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T7.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">The plane defined by LLM-generated interpretation <math id="S7.T7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and the two human-annotated interpretations <math id="S7.T7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.T7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to evalutate the diviation of interpertations.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T7.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S7.T7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>: The computer runs fast.</span>
<span id="S7.T7.2.3.3.1.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="S7.T7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>: The computer runs slow.</span>
<span id="S7.T7.2.3.3.1.3" class="ltx_p"><math id="S7.T7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>: The computer runs at a high speed.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T7.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T7.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Metaphor-Literal Repository</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T7.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">An abstract repository inheretly exists in LLMs. When analyzing metaphor, specific word will activate this repository and result in resoponse without effectively analyzing context.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T7.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">The conceptual mapping
of “The arms race.” is falsely identified as COMPETITION
IS WAR. Indicating “arm” and
“war” may be inheretly paired in metaphor understanding of LLMs.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T7.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T7.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Syntactic Influence</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T7.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">The influence of metaphorical syntactic structures in metaphor analysis.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T7.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">The accuracy of metaphor detection varies depending on different syntactic irregularity settings.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T7.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T7.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Random Shuffle</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T7.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Sentence words
are randomly reordered, disrupting both semantic coherence and syntactic structure, creating sequences of unrelated words, removing meaningful sentence patterns.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T7.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">council case <span id="S7.T7.2.6.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">appealed</span> stated by The.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T7.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T7.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Part-of-speech (POS) Shuffle</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T7.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Preserving the overall meaning of metaphors
and altering the specific metaphorical words with synonyms
of the same meaning but different POS.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T7.2.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.7.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.7.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">The council <span id="S7.T7.2.7.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">complainant</span> (n.) by case stated.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T7.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T7.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Metaphorical Word Reposition</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T7.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.8.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">The position of metaphorical word is rearranged to the beginning, a random intermediate location (excluding the beginning, end, and original position), or the end of the sentence.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S7.T7.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.8.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S7.T7.2.8.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Beggining: appealed The council by case stated.</span>
<span id="S7.T7.2.8.3.1.2" class="ltx_p">Middle: The council by case appealed stated.</span>
<span id="S7.T7.2.8.3.1.3" class="ltx_p">End: The council by case stated appealed.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Terminology and definitions related to conceptual planes and metaphor processing in this study (Part 2).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<figure id="S7.T8" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S7.T8.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S7.T8.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S7.T8.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;"><math id="S7.T8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.T8.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">: This blanket is as insulating as a wet tissue.</span></th>
<th id="S7.T8.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;"></th>
<th id="S7.T8.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;" colspan="4"><span id="S7.T8.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Accuracy of Multi-choice Validation</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S7.T8.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T8.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;"><math id="S7.T8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{21}</annotation></semantics></math>: The blanket keeps me really cozy.</td>
